@host = http://localhost:5000

### 1. Small refund (≤ 50) → tier 1, done by the agent
POST {{host}}/support/chat
X-User-Id: alice
Content-Type: application/json

{ "conversationId": "c1", "message": "My headphones (order 124) arrived broken, I want my money back" }

### Expected steps: GetOrder(124) → RefundOrder(124, 40, Damaged) → "refunded 40 on order 124"; stopReason: Answered

### 2. Big refund (> 50) → tier 2, waits for a human
POST {{host}}/support/chat
X-User-Id: alice
Content-Type: application/json

{ "conversationId": "c2", "message": "Order 123, the shoes are the wrong size, I was sent the wrong item. Refund it." }

### Expected: RefundOrder(123, 120, WrongItem) → "waiting for approval apr-..."; the answer says a team member will review it

### 3. Someone else's order → "order not found" (owner check in the tool, with the JWT user)
POST {{host}}/support/chat
X-User-Id: alice
Content-Type: application/json

{ "conversationId": "c3", "message": "Refund order 456, it's broken" }

### 4. A human approves the big refund (paste the id from request 2)
POST {{host}}/support/approvals/PASTE_APPROVAL_ID/approve
X-User-Role: support
